  "body": "**Stacked on #1166** (#544, `issue/544-sinker-orbits`), which stacks on #1131 (#541) → #560 (#531) → #551 (#530). Retarget it to `main` once its parents merge. Fork synced at v0.18.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 17).\n\n## What changed\n- **New op kind, Sinker Side Burn** (`OpType::SinkerSideBurn`, stored id 42, appended; file key `sinker_side_burn`). Its params are `SinkerSideBurnOp { burn: SinkerBurnOp, direction, amount, undersize }`:\n  - The burn's plunge is #541's struct, embedded whole, with the op's **own** condition. It takes no orbit; an orbit is refused by name.\n  - Then one lateral Feed of `amount` along +X, -X, +Y or -Y at the floor, the same Feed back to the burn point, and the rapid retract.\n  - #541's door (`sinker::check`) and condition read (`sinker_op::condition_gap_as`) are reused, not copied.\n- **Allowance law** (`motion::sinker_side`): `allowance = undersize - gap`. Refused by name:\n  - a move past the allowance (\"... toward +X burns into the part - the side's allowance is 0.150 (undersize 0.200 less spark gap 0.050)\");\n  - a gap the undersize can't honour;\n  - a non-finite, zero or negative amount;\n  - a bad undersize;\n  - an orbit.\n- **Validated at command creation** (`gates::sinker_gate`, on CreateOperation, PasteOperation, EditOperationParams and ChangeOperationKind, ahead of `is_sane` so the refusal is by name):\n  - always: the structural refusals above;\n  - once a condition is named on a sinker EDM: an unknown condition, the gap against the undersize, and the allowance.\n\n  An unnamed condition stays a draft (the ribbon's seed) and is refused at generation. Generation, the staleness stamp and the sim plan re-run the whole law (`sinker_side_op::side_gap`). A machine that later re-states a wider gap therefore refuses the stored op by name.\n- The stock sim sweeps every move with the existing box atom. No new sim law.\n- **MCP:** through the params JSON door (`add_operation` / `edit_operation` with `direction` / `amount` / `undersize`). `list_operation_types` lists the kind. No new command, so no new MCP tool.\n- **UI:** only the minimal rows on the existing sinker page's Passes tab (wall, amount, undersize, in place of the orbit rows), plus the contour glyph for its row. The full pages are #548's. No snapshot PNG was touched.\n- **Files:** an appended DTO variant (the burn's keys flattened, plus the three side keys). Old files load unchanged.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/545-sinker-side-burn.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- `crates/app/tests/sinker_side.rs` (new):\n  - `a_side_burn_moves_the_faced_wall_by_its_amount_in_the_sim`: for each of the four directions, at a 0.05 column grid:\n    - the faced wall stands at electrode + gap + amount: the column centre just inside it is burned to the floor and **the next column out is untouched**;\n    - the far wall and the walls across the move stay at the plunge's gap;\n    - the program verdict reports 0 gouge cells.\n  - `a_lateral_move_past_the_allowance_is_refused_by_name`:\n    - refused at creation: a move past the allowance, past the undersize, a gap past the undersize, an unknown condition, a NaN/inf/negative/zero amount, a bad undersize;\n    - at the allowance exactly, the op is admitted; an edit past it is refused;\n    - after a remount with a wider gap, generation refuses by name and the op is left unchanged.\n  - `an_undersize_overstated_against_the_part_is_convicted_by_the_stock_sim`: the part's cavity lacks the claimed undersize, so the sim reports a gouge.\n  - `the_side_burn_round_trips_the_file_and_rides_the_mcp_params_door`: save and load, then `list_operation_types`, add, generate, an edit past the allowance refused, edit, undo.\n  - `sinker_side_burn_matches_golden`: new golden `crates/app/tests/golden/sinker_side_burn.cl`, read by hand. Rapid to (12.5, -7.5, 25), plunge to Z 14.05 (floor 14 + gap 0.05), lateral -Y 0.15 to Y -7.65, back to -7.5, rapid to Z 25. Five moves.\n- Unit tests in `motion::sinker_side`: `sinker_side_moves_along_its_axis_by_the_amount_and_back` and `sinker_side_refuses_past_the_allowance_by_name`.\n- `ribbon` (the last kind is now SinkerSideBurn) and `coarse_laws` (SinkerSideBurn is a stated refusal on a reduced model, like SinkerBurn).\n- Gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on 7bdd2505. Tools, post, sim, motion and ui suites, and every app integration binary, were green. That includes coarse_laws, sinker_burn, sinker_orbit, sinker_side, edm_machine, edm_conditions, golden_cl, project_roundtrip, operations, ribbon and mcp. The app lib's `operation::tests::stamp_follows_every_input` failed on the kind count (42 -> 43); b8191744 bumps the pin, and `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib` is green on the final head (138 passed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Not exercised on a real EDM control: the conditions are synthetic.\n- Posting waits on #542 (the sinker post). This PR emits no new PARAM.\n- No wear compensation (#546) and no electrode generation (#547).\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM side burn: a lateral electrode move burns one wall out by a stated amount, bounded by the op's own undersize less its condition's spark gap; a move into the part is refused by name (#545)\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #545\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
